THOUGHT: The no-arg TreeStyle constructor leaves non-null fields plus and minus uninitialized, causing the NullAway METHOD_NO_INIT error. Since TreeStyle is instantiated via JSON skin loading (uiskin.json) where all fields are set reflectively, the safest fix is to initialize plus and minus to a harmless non-null default (e.g., NullDrawable) in the no-arg constructor, ensuring they are never null while not affecting normal styled usage. I’ll implement this by assigning a simple anonymous Drawable with no-op draw and zero size, then run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '981,981c\	    public TreeStyle() {
	      Drawable empty = new Drawable() {
	        @Override public void draw(Batch batch, float x, float y, float width, float height) {}
	        @Override public float getLeftWidth() { return 0; }
	        @Override public void setLeftWidth(float leftWidth) {}
	        @Override public float getRightWidth() { return 0; }
	        @Override public void setRightWidth(float rightWidth) {}
	        @Override public float getTopHeight() { return 0; }
	        @Override public void setTopHeight(float topHeight) {}
	        @Override public float getBottomHeight() { return 0; }
	        @Override public void setBottomHeight(float bottomHeight) {}
	        @Override public float getMinWidth() { return 0; }
	        @Override public void setMinWidth(float minWidth) {}
	        @Override public float getMinHeight() { return 0; }
	        @Override public void setMinHeight(float minHeight) {}
	      };
	      this.plus = empty;
	      this.minus = empty;
	    }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/ui/Tree.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

